______________________________________________________________________

# 11. RMSSD Threshold Semantics

The matrix uses:

$$
>
$$

so the literal threshold condition is:

$$
RMSSD>35ms
$$

not:

$$
RMSSD\ge35ms.
$$

Boundary behavior:

```yaml
rmssd_boundary:

  threshold:
    35

  unit:
    ms

  operator:
    STRICT_GREATER_THAN

  examples:

    34.9:
      invariant_satisfied: false

    35.0:
      invariant_satisfied: false

    35.1:
      invariant_satisfied: true
```

Again, this is merely the mathematics of the source expression.

It does not establish that 35 ms is a universal clinical threshold.

______________________________________________________________________

# 12. Vagal Tone vs HRV

The row title is:

```text
Vagal Tone (HRV)
```

This explicitly associates the two constructs inside the source model.

However:

$$
VagalTone
=
HRV
$$

should not automatically be treated as a universal physiological identity outside the AMOS model.

The source establishes an architectural association:

$$
VagalTone
\leftrightarrow
HRVTelemetry
$$

within this artifact.

The exact computation of `Vagal Tone` is not supplied.

______________________________________________________________________

# 13. Cognitive Load De-escalation

The anomaly action is:

```text
Cognitive Load De-escalation
```

This creates a direct biological-to-cognitive governance edge:

$$
HRVAnomaly
\rightarrow
CognitiveLoadDeEscalation
$$

At the AMOS model level, this is significant because biological telemetry is not treated solely as passive observation.

It is given permission to alter cognitive load policy.

That means the source architecture expresses:

$$
\boxed{
BiologicalState
\rightarrow
CognitivePacingPolicy
}
$$

as a **model-level routing contract**.

It does not independently establish that real physiological HRV causes computational reasoning degradation in the exact way modeled.

______________________________________________________________________

# 14. Relation to UBI × Full Brain

The previously supplied UBI × Full Brain matrix contains:

```text
Layer 5
Biological Integration
Autonomic vagal telemetry
Distress Veto (τ < 0.20)
```

The Full Brain specification additionally says that Full Brain governance links cognitive processing with:

```text
UBI biological pacing
and
vagal coherence
```

The current NeuroSyncAI matrix supplies a more concrete vagal telemetry row:

$$
VagalTone/HRV
\rightarrow
RMSSD
\rightarrow
CognitiveLoadDeEscalation
$$

This yields a strong candidate hierarchy:

```text
VAGAL TELEMETRY
      │
      ▼
HRV / RMSSD SIGNAL
      │
      ▼
VAGAL COHERENCE / BIOLOGICAL PACING
      │
      ▼
COGNITIVE LOAD GOVERNANCE
```

But the exact edges remain partly derived.

Specifically, the matrix does not state:

$$
RMSSD
\rightarrow
\tau_{bio}
$$

nor:

$$
RMSSD
=
\tau
$$

nor:

$$
CognitiveLoadDeEscalation
=
DistressVeto.
$$

Those must remain separate until the binding specifies them.

______________________________________________________________________

# 15. Local De-escalation vs Distress Veto

A useful source-safe distinction is:

```text
RMSSD anomaly
→ Cognitive Load De-escalation
```

versus:

```text
τ < 0.20
→ Distress Veto
```

The first looks like a **corrective pacing response**.

The second looks like a **stronger veto response**.

Therefore a possible escalation architecture is:

$$
Warning
\rightarrow
DeEscalation
\rightarrow
Veto
$$

but this is not explicitly stated.

It remains a **DERIVED candidate**.

