# 26. Relationship to UBI Four-Domain Model

The supplied UBI framework defines four source-model domains:

```text
NBI — Neurobiological Intelligence
NEI — Neuroemotional Intelligence
SI  — Somatic Intelligence
BEI — Bioelectromagnetic Intelligence
```

The NeuroSyncAI telemetry channels appear structurally relatable to these domains, but the matrix does not explicitly assign them.

A candidate mapping is:

| NeuroSyncAI signal  | Candidate UBI relationship | Status            |
| ------------------- | -------------------------- | ----------------- |
| EEG Gamma Coherence | NBI / BEI                  | COMPETING         |
| Vagal Tone / HRV    | NEI / BEI                  | COMPETING         |
| GSR / Electrodermal | NEI                        | DERIVED candidate |

It would be unsafe to force:

```text
EEG = BEI
HRV = NEI
GSR = SI
```

or any other one-to-one mapping without the binding.

UBI is explicitly non-compensatory and multidomain in the supplied source model, so signals may participate in more than one domain.

______________________________________________________________________

# 27. Relationship to UBI Biological Alignment

Earlier supplied UBI content defines:

$$
i
=
(NBI\cdot NEI\cdot SI\cdot BEI)^{1/4}
$$

and:

$$
e=i^2.
$$

The current matrix does **not** specify how EEG, HRV, or GSR values contribute numerically to:

$$
NBI,
NEI,
SI,
BEI
$$

or to:

$$
i.
$$

Therefore the following mapping is missing:

$$
Telemetry
\rightarrow
DomainScore
\rightarrow
i
\rightarrow
e.
$$

That is a decision-relevant gap.

Do not infer a direct formula such as:

$$
BEI=PhaseSync
$$

or:

$$
NEI=RMSSD
$$

or:

$$
SI=GSR
$$

without explicit source support.

______________________________________________________________________

# 28. Relationship to UBI × Cognition

The UBI × Cognition artifacts supplied earlier define:

```text
NBI → Working Memory Allocator
NEI → Tone & Communication Filter
SI → Execution Throttle
BEI → 40Hz Gamma Clock Synchronizer
```

with adaptive actions including:

```text
Context Compaction
Safety Communication Mask
Batch Rate Limiting
Agent Resynchronization Pulse
```

The NeuroSyncAI matrix can therefore be interpreted as providing a possible telemetry surface feeding those higher-level cognitive controls.

Candidate topology:

```text
BIOLOGICAL SIGNAL
      ↓
NEUROSYNCAI TELEMETRY
      ↓
SIGNAL INVARIANT
      ↓
UBI STATE
      ↓
COGNITIVE POLICY
```

But only the NeuroSyncAI telemetry and local actions are directly source-defined here.

The intermediate mapping:

$$
NeuroSyncAI
\rightarrow
UBIDomainState
$$

must come from the binding.

______________________________________________________________________

# 29. Relationship to UBI × Emotion

UBI × Emotion provides an affective state vector:

$$
\vec E_t
=
\langle
Valence,
Arousal,
Dominance
\rangle.
$$

NeuroSyncAI contains:

```text
Vagal Tone / HRV
GSR / Electrodermal
```

which could act as inputs to affective state modeling.

However the source does not provide equations:

$$
v_t=f(HRV,GSR)
$$

$$
a_t=g(HRV,GSR)
$$

$$
d_t=h(HRV,GSR).
$$

Therefore those functions remain:

```text
UNKNOWN
```

and should not be invented.

______________________________________________________________________

# 30. Relationship to UBI × Full Brain

UBI × Full Brain identifies whole-system biological pacing and vagal coherence.

The NeuroSyncAI matrix provides concrete source-defined signals that are plausible inputs to that layer:

```text
EEG Gamma Coherence
Vagal Tone / HRV
GSR
```

A candidate hierarchy is:

```text
SENSORS / TELEMETRY
        ↓
NEUROSYNCAI
        ↓
UBI BIOLOGICAL STATE
        ↓
FULL BRAIN GOVERNANCE
        ↓
COGNITIVE ACTION
```

This is one of the strongest architecture-level interpretations available from the supplied materials.

Nevertheless, the exact transport protocol, state schema, signal fusion, and authorization boundary are absent.

______________________________________________________________________

# 31. Relationship to NeuroSyncAI Canon

The Drive corpus contains a dedicated document titled **“UBI + NeuroSyncAI Integration Framework Across the GCBAT Ecosystem”**, showing that UBI–NeuroSyncAI integration exists as an explicit framework family in the source corpus.

The Drive corpus also contains dedicated NeuroSyncAI architecture material, including **“NeuroSyncAI_Dual-System_Architecture_for_Biological_Recovery_and_Integrity_Enforcement.md”**.

A separate exact-title search for `UBI_NEUROSYNCAI_BINDING` did not surface an accessible file under that exact name, so the binding artifact should remain an unresolved dependency rather than be treated as retrieved canon.

This means the current matrix has **corpus-level integration support**, but its precise binding semantics remain incomplete.

______________________________________________________________________

# 32. NeuroSyncAI Dual-System Hypothesis

Because the corpus contains a document explicitly named:

```text
NeuroSyncAI Dual-System Architecture
for Biological Recovery and Integrity Enforcement
```

a likely source architecture may involve separate:

```text
RECOVERY
```

and:

```text
INTEGRITY ENFORCEMENT
```

functions.

However, the current matrix itself does not define those two systems.

Therefore any direct assignment such as:

```text
Frequency Re-Pacing = Recovery System
RMSSD Guard = Integrity System
```

would be speculative.

The only safe conclusion is:

```text
RELATED SOURCE FAMILY EXISTS
```

not:

```text
CURRENT ROWS HAVE PROVEN DUAL-SYSTEM ASSIGNMENTS
```

______________________________________________________________________

# 33. Signal-Invariant Contract

The matrix treats each telemetry channel as having an invariant.

This produces a generic form:

$$
I_i(S_i)
\in
\{PASS,FAIL\}
$$

where:

$$
I_{\gamma}(S)
=
PhaseSync>0.65
$$

$$
I_{HRV}(S)
=
RMSSD>35ms
$$

$$
I_{GSR}(S)
=
TonicDrift<1.5\mu S/min.
$$

Then:

$$
FAIL(I_i)
\Rightarrow
A_i.
$$

This is the cleanest deterministic normalization of the source.

______________________________________________________________________

# 34. Missing Hysteresis

No release thresholds are provided.

For example, the source specifies:

$$
PhaseSync>0.65
$$

but not:

```text
after re-pacing:
when does re-pacing stop?
```

Likewise:

$$
RMSSD>35ms
$$

does not define:

```text
when is cognitive load restored?
```

and:

$$
TonicDrift<1.5\mu S/min
$$

does not define:

```text
when is stress cool-down released?
```

Without separate entry and exit thresholds, a real controller could oscillate around a threshold.

This is an **implementation gap**, not a criticism of the source model.

Canonical status:

```yaml
hysteresis:
  NOT_DEFINED
```

______________________________________________________________________

# 35. Missing Temporal Window

The matrix does not define how long a violation must persist.

Examples:

$$
PhaseSync=0.64
$$

for:

```text
1 millisecond?
1 second?
30 seconds?
```

is not distinguished.

Similarly:

$$
RMSSD=34ms
$$

for one transient measurement may or may not constitute an anomaly.

Therefore every signal invariant lacks an explicit:

$$
\Delta t_{validation}
$$

or observation window.

This is a material runtime gap.

______________________________________________________________________

# 36. Missing Sampling Rate

The matrix provides signal frequency bands but not sensor sample rates.

These are different concepts.

A source-safe controller still needs:

```yaml
sampling_rate:
  UNKNOWN

window_length:
  UNKNOWN

filter_order:
  UNKNOWN

artifact_rejection:
  UNKNOWN

missing_data_policy:
  UNKNOWN
```

None should be fabricated.

______________________________________________________________________

# 37. Missing Calibration

The matrix does not establish whether thresholds are:

- universal;
- individual baseline-relative;
- cohort-normalized;
- device-specific;
- session-calibrated;
- age-adjusted;
- context-dependent.

Therefore:

```text
THRESHOLD VALUE
!=
CALIBRATION PROTOCOL
```

and:

```yaml
calibration:
  UNKNOWN_GAP
```

______________________________________________________________________

# 38. Missing Confidence / Signal Quality

No signal-quality condition is supplied.

A robust telemetry architecture normally needs to distinguish:

$$
SignalAnomaly
$$

from:

$$
SensorFailure
$$

or:

$$
Artifact.
$$

But the current artifact does not define that distinction.

Therefore:

$$
Anomaly
\stackrel{?}{=}
BiologicalAnomaly
$$

is not guaranteed.

A future binding should ideally distinguish:

```text
VALID SIGNAL + OUT-OF-INVARIANT
```

from:

```text
INVALID SIGNAL
```

and:

```text
MISSING SIGNAL
```

and:

```text
STALE SIGNAL.
```

______________________________________________________________________

# 39. Freshness Requirement

No freshness field is present.

Yet biological telemetry is intrinsically time-indexed in the model.

A source-safe runtime representation should therefore preserve:

```yaml
timestamp:
freshness:
signal_age:
```

but the acceptance threshold for signal age is not known.

Thus:

```text
FRESHNESS POLICY = UNKNOWN
```

______________________________________________________________________

# 40. Provenance Requirement

Each telemetry observation should conceptually retain provenance:

```text
sensor/source identity
measurement timestamp
processing pipeline
calibration state
signal quality
derivation history
```

This is a **DERIVED RSCF requirement**, consistent with AMOS provenance discipline.

It is not explicitly spelled out in the three-row matrix.

______________________________________________________________________

# 41. Source Independence

Multiple derived signals from the same physical stream must not automatically count as independent evidence.

For example:

```text
EEG gamma amplitude
EEG gamma phase
EEG gamma coherence
```

could all share one sensor ancestry.

Thus:

$$
3\ metrics
\neq
3\ independent\ provenance\ roots.
$$

This matters if NeuroSyncAI later combines signals into confidence estimates.

The current matrix does not define a fusion-confidence rule.

______________________________________________________________________

# 42. Cross-Signal Correlation

EEG, HRV, and GSR may be treated as separate telemetry streams in the matrix.

That does not establish statistical independence.

Therefore:

$$
EEG\perp HRV\perp GSR
$$

must **not** be assumed.

The model should preserve:

```yaml
provenance_independence:
  NOT_ESTABLISHED

statistical_independence:
  NOT_ESTABLISHED
```

______________________________________________________________________

# 43. Signal Fusion

No canonical fusion equation is provided.

Thus there is no source support for formulas such as:

$$
NeuroSyncScore
=
w_1\gamma+w_2HRV+w_3GSR
$$

or:

$$
CoherenceIndex
=
(\gamma\cdot HRV\cdot GSR)^{1/3}.
$$

Those would be inventions.

The matrix defines three channel-local invariants, not a unified NeuroSync score.

______________________________________________________________________

# 44. Non-Compensatory Interpretation

The wider UBI model is described as non-compensatory.

If that principle applies here, one failing telemetry channel might not be allowed to be “cancelled out” by strong performance on another.

However the current matrix does not explicitly state:

$$
Pass(EEG)
+
Pass(HRV)
\Rightarrow
IgnoreFail(GSR).
$$

Nor does it state the opposite.

Therefore the non-compensatory behavior of this specific matrix remains a **candidate inheritance from UBI**, not an explicit local law.

______________________________________________________________________

# 45. Candidate Fail-Closed Principle

The matrix actions are corrective rather than destructive:

```text
RE-PACE
DE-ESCALATE
COOL DOWN
```

Therefore the immediate architecture appears to prefer reversible intervention.

A candidate policy is:

$$
Anomaly
\Rightarrow
MinimalLocalCorrection
$$

before:

$$
GlobalHalt.
$$

This is consistent with AMOS governance principles but is not directly asserted in the matrix.

