______________________________________________________________________

# 62. Governance Boundary

The telemetry matrix provides signals.

Signals do not grant authority.

Therefore:

$$
Telemetry
\neq
Authority.
$$

A measured anomaly may license a source-defined adaptive response inside the model, but it must not be silently generalized into:

```text
legal authority
medical authority
employment authority
disciplinary authority
identity judgment
moral judgment
```

without separate governance.

This preserves:

$$
\boxed{
Capability\neq Authority
}
$$

and:

$$
\boxed{
Observation\neq Authorization
}
$$

______________________________________________________________________

# 63. Privacy Boundary

Because the artifact concerns biological telemetry, any executable implementation would require explicit data-governance policy.

The matrix itself does not define:

- consent;
- retention;
- deletion;
- access control;
- sharing;
- secondary use;
- anonymization;
- encryption;
- jurisdiction;
- user override.

Therefore:

```yaml
privacy_governance:
  NOT_DEFINED_IN_THIS_ARTIFACT
```

This is an implementation-critical gap, but not a reason to alter the source matrix itself.

