# 65. Deterministic Evaluation Function — Derived

A minimal deterministic representation is:

$$
Evaluate_{\gamma}(x)
=
\begin{cases}
PASS,&x>0.65\\
ANOMALY,&x\le0.65
\end{cases}
$$

$$
Evaluate_{HRV}(r)
=
\begin{cases}
PASS,&r>35ms\\
ANOMALY,&r\le35ms
\end{cases}
$$

$$
Evaluate_{GSR}(d)
=
\begin{cases}
PASS,&d<1.5\mu S/min\\
ANOMALY,&d\ge1.5\mu S/min
\end{cases}
$$

Then:

$$
Route(ANOMALY_\gamma)
=
FrequencyRePacing
$$

$$
Route(ANOMALY_{HRV})
=
CognitiveLoadDeEscalation
$$

$$
Route(ANOMALY_{GSR})
=
StressCoolDownTrigger.
$$

This is a direct mathematical normalization of the table.

______________________________________________________________________

# 66. Important Caveat on “Invariant”

The matrix labels these rules:

```text
Signal Invariant
```

That term should be preserved.

But it does not necessarily mean a mathematical invariant in the strict sense of a conserved quantity.

Within this artifact, `Signal Invariant` functions operationally as a:

```text
required admissible signal condition
```

or:

```text
acceptance envelope.
```

The exact canonical ontology of `Invariant` should come from the matrix specification or binding.

______________________________________________________________________

