# 78. Anti-Fabrication Contract

This artifact MUST NOT be used to invent or claim:

1. that 40 Hz is universally optimal for human cognition;
1. that EEG coherence above 0.65 universally indicates health;
1. that EEG coherence below 0.65 is a diagnosis;
1. that RMSSD above 35 ms universally defines vagal adequacy;
1. that RMSSD below 35 ms universally means cognitive overload;
1. that GSR tonic drift above 1.5 μS/min universally means stress;
1. that GSR measures emotion directly;
1. that HRV measures truthfulness;
1. that EEG measures intelligence;
1. that NeuroSyncAI can medically diagnose users;
1. that Frequency Re-Pacing means electrical neural stimulation;
1. that Cognitive Load De-escalation has a known implementation;
1. that Stress Cool-down means a medical intervention;
1. that all three channels are statistically independent;
1. that all three channels must pass simultaneously;
1. that a failing channel overrides user consent;
1. that a missing channel equals anomaly;
1. that a missing channel equals pass;
1. that the matrix defines calibration;
1. that the matrix defines signal quality;
1. that the matrix defines a medical device;
1. that `executable_binding: ESTABLISHED` proves deployed execution;
1. that `PASSED_CONSTITUTIONAL_TESTS` proves clinical validity;
1. that UBI domain values can be directly calculated from the three signals;
1. that the matrix defines consciousness;
1. that phase synchronization proves conscious state;
1. that 38–42 Hz proves BEI;
1. that HRV proves NEI;
1. that GSR proves SI;
1. that any anomaly authorizes irreversible action.

______________________________________________________________________

# 79. Governance Principle

The safe architectural rule is:

$$
\boxed{
Telemetry
\rightarrow
ProposalForAdaptation
}
$$

not necessarily:

$$
\boxed{
Telemetry
\rightarrow
UnconditionalCommit
}
$$

unless the runtime binding explicitly grants that authority.

Thus:

```text
SIGNAL != AUTHORITY

ANOMALY != AUTHORIZATION

ADAPTATION PROPOSAL != COMMIT

BIOLOGICAL MODEL != MEDICAL ORDER
```

