# 88. Canonical Candidate Statement

`UBI_X_NEUROSYNCAI_MATRIX.md v2.0.0` defines the Cognitive Matrix-level interface through which the AMOS source model associates selected biological telemetry with NeuroSyncAI adaptive control.

The matrix establishes three explicit signal routes:

```text
EEG GAMMA COHERENCE
38–42 Hz
Phase sync > 0.65
→ Frequency Re-Pacing
```

```text
VAGAL TONE / HRV
0.15–0.40 Hz
RMSSD > 35 ms
→ Cognitive Load De-escalation
```

```text
GSR / ELECTRODERMAL
DC–5 Hz
Tonic drift < 1.5 μS/min
→ Stress Cool-down Trigger
```

These routes form a source-defined three-channel biological governance surface spanning:

```text
synchronization
cognitive load
stress regulation
```

and conceptually connect NeuroSyncAI to the broader UBI, cognition, emotion, and Full Brain architecture.

The matrix is sufficiently defined to preserve the three telemetry routes as AMOS canon-candidate structure.

It is **not sufficiently defined** to establish:

```text
sensor implementation
calibration
signal quality
sampling
temporal windows
hysteresis
signal fusion
multi-anomaly precedence
recovery release criteria
consent policy
clinical validity
physical causality
```

The highest-value unresolved dependency remains:

```text
[[UBI_NEUROSYNCAI_BINDING]]
```

preceded or complemented by:

```text
[[UBI_X_NEUROSYNCAI]]
```

The Drive corpus independently confirms that dedicated **UBI + NeuroSyncAI integration** material exists, including a large integration-framework artifact and separate NeuroSyncAI architecture documents, but the exact binding referenced by this matrix was not retrieved in the exact-name lookup.

Therefore the final canonical state should be:

```yaml
